# Theory derivation standard

When writing or revising theory (`THEORY.md`, `THEORY_PROGRAM_DEGREE.md`, proofs, taxonomy claims):

## Required style

Do **not** state a reduction, absorption step, or program-degree claim as a slogan.
For every nontrivial claim, give an **explicit derivation** in the latent / response-function model:

1. **SCM / graph** — structural equations and independence among latents.
2. **Query** — expand \(Q\) as a sum over the latents that actually appear (e.g. \(P(Y_x)=\sum_u \mathbf{1}[f_Y(x,u)=y]P(u)\)).
3. **Observational map** — expand \(P(v)\) (or \(P(v\mid\cdot)\)) as a sum over all latents.
4. **Elimination** — show precisely why a latent or simplex factor drops out (Q-irrelevant, pinned by a margin, or projected via conditionals), with the reduced program written in full.
5. **Degree readout** — count free simplex factors left in the reduced program.

## Canonical template (IV-style)

Use this pattern throughout (adapt graph/assumptions):

```text
Setup:   Z=f_Z(U_Z), X=f_X(Z,U), Y=f_Y(X,U), U_Z ⊥ U
Query:   P(Y_x=y) = ∑_u 1[f_Y(x,u)=y] P(U=u)     ← no U_Z
Data:    P(z,x,y) = P(z) · P(x,y|z)
         P(x,y|z) = ∑_u 1[f_X(z,u)=x]1[f_Y(x,u)=y] P(U=u)
Reduce:  opt over P(U) s.t. conditionals match; P(U_Z)=P(Z) pinned
Degree:  1 (LP in q^{XY})
```

## Coverage

Illustrate **each** theorem / corollary with at least one such derivation, varying:

- graphs (order-only, bow, IV, extended IV, pair-chain latents, Markovian, triangle, …);
- queries (interventional, PNS/PN, multi-regime joints, conditionals);
- assumptions (faces/MTR, exclusions, independence splits, anchored MSM).

Distinguish **pinning absorption** (factor identified from \(P\)) from **Q-irrelevant elimination** (factor not in \(Q\); constraints project onto the rest).

## Do not

- Invoke “WL–WR / instrument cut” or “absorption” without expanding \(Q\) and \(P\).
- Treat package routing heuristics as proofs.
- Leave “by c-factorization” as the only justification for dropping a latent.
